# Factory-level credentials: what the factory MACHINE itself needs, once, for every app it runs.
# This file is a sample of NAMES only. Never fill it in and never commit a filled copy.
# Each value lives in the place named on its line, set the way described in docs/CREDENTIALS.md.

# --- Sign-ins (no value to store: run the command once on the factory machine) ---------------------------
# GitHub CLI, to read CI results and open pull requests:        gh auth login
# Vercel CLI, to deploy Vercel apps:                            vercel login
# SSH key per self-hosted app (~/.ssh/<ssh_key_ref>), made by:  python3 .claude/scripts/provision.py <app> --qualify-remote

# --- Uptime alerts (lives in ~/.config/software-factory/uptime.env, mode 600) ----------------------------
# A Resend API key with "Sending access" for your notification domain. Set it with:
#   python3 .claude/scripts/uptime.py set-email-key
RESEND_API_KEY=re_xxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx
# Optional: who the alert comes from (default: Software factory <alerts@<notify_domain>>)
UPTIME_EMAIL_FROM="Software factory <alerts@yourcompany.com>"

# --- Coding agents for benchmarks (optional; each agent's own login, run once) ---------------------------
# Claude Code: claude (sign in)    Codex: codex login --device-auth    Cursor: agent login    Pi: pi, then /login
# Others: see docs/AGENT_INTEGRATION.md (each agent's auth env var name)

# --- Not credentials, but private: state/factory.local.json (copy state/factory.local.example.json) -------
# operator_email, notify_domain, vercel_team, the factory machine's address, mold_sources
